    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall only be used for a purpose ancillary or incidental, or both, to the residential use of the dwelling house currently known as 106 Leatherhead Road Chessington KT9 2HY as set out in the submitted application form signed 25.11.2025, unless otherwise first agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: The proposal has been assessed as householder development and were the habitable accommodation to be used as a separate unit of accommodation this would have implications for neighbouring amenity, standard of accommodation and levels of on-site car parking.",
    "The works shall be carried out and maintained in accordance with the deposited Fire Statement compliant with Policy D12(A).\r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users in accordance with Policy D12 (Fire Safety) of the London Plan 2021."
